function settingsView(){return `${header('AUTHORING SETTINGS','Storysmith AI','Connect an OpenAI-compatible endpoint for build-time content generation.') }<section class="panel" style="max-width:650px"><div class="panel-heading"><h3>OpenAI-compatible API</h3><span class="badge">CHAT COMPLETIONS</span></div><p class="small-copy">The assistant runs only when you build your world. Generated entities stay a draft until you keep them. The API key is read from the workbench environment, never saved in the world database, and never included in exports.</p><div class="form-field"><label>BASE URL</label><input class="input" id="api-base" placeholder="https://api.example.com/v1"></div><div class="form-field"><label>MODEL ID</label><input class="input" id="api-model" placeholder="model-name"></div><div class="prompt-row" style="margin-top:14px">API key: <b id="key-status">Set MUDMAKER_OPENAI_API_KEY in the private Compose environment.</b> Keep it in an untracked <code>.env</code> file.</div><div class="form-field"><label><input type="checkbox" class="toggle" id="api-json-mode"> Request JSON mode (when supported by the provider)</label></div><div class="modal-actions"><button class="button button-primary" id="save-settings">Save settings</button></div></section><section class="panel" style="max-width:650px;margin-top:13px"><h3 style="font:700 13px Manrope;margin:0 0 8px">Scaffold completion</h3><p class="small-copy">Give the assistant an entity type, any fields you already have, and an instruction such as “add a secret rumor and a quest hook.” It returns a structured entity you can review, edit, and apply.</p><div class="prompt-row">Supported starters: NPC, quest, crafting recipe, vendor, room, item, biome, dialogue, description, world, and custom entities.</div></section><section class="panel" style="max-width:650px;margin-top:13px"><div class="panel-heading"><h3>AI clients with MCP</h3><span class="badge">CREATOR + GAME MASTER</span></div><p class="small-copy">Connect an MCP client to the creator to read and edit worlds, complete scaffolds, paint maps, playtest, and export. Exported games also include a Game Master server for player management, announcements, and special events.</p><div class="prompt-row">Default local endpoints:<br>Creator: <code>http://localhost:8082/mcp</code><br>Exported game: <code>http://localhost:2223/mcp</code></div><p class="small-copy">Each server requires its own bearer token. Tokens are generated privately in its persistent volume, or supplied through the Compose environment. See README.md for connection commands. Event drafts are validated before activation; rewards and event history persist across restarts.</p></section>`}
